    {
      "pool_size": 25,
      "pool_returned": 25,
      "candidates": [
        {
          "entry_id": 2733,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.47166866,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What are your clinic hours and locations?\nAnswer: We are open Monday through Saturday from 9:00 AM to 6:00 PM at 15a Willson St. The nearest free parking is a 3-minute walk away at the Mega Mall parking garage (9 Willson St.).",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2728,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.4044399,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Do you offer virtual or telehealth consultations?\nAnswer: No, we currently only offer in-person visits at our clinic location.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2742,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.30493617,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Your privacy and your health information\n\n## Who can see your medical record\n\nYour record can be seen only by the practitioners and staff involved in your care at the clinic, and by the staff who handle billing for your visits. We share information from your record with your insurance company only as far as is needed to process claims for your care. We never share your health information with your employer, and we never sell it.\n\n## Conversations with the chat assistant\n\nConversations with the clinic's chat assistant are kept with your appointment records. Clinic staff can read them, and a staff member may join a conversation to help you. Do not use the chat to report a medical emergency: call 911 or go to the nearest emergency department.\n\n## Recording a consultation\n\nYou may make an audio recording of your own consultation for your personal use, as long as you tell the practitioner before you start. Staff and other patients must not be recorded or photographed.\n\n",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2734,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.30461186,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: How early should I arrive before my scheduled appointment time?\nAnswer: If it is your first visit to our clinic, please arrive 15 minutes before your appointment time to complete your registration paperwork. Returning patients can arrive 5 to 10 minutes prior to their slot.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2740,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.29663488,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "only the clinic's name, a callback number and your first name - never the reason for the call or any health details.\n\n## Messages we will never send\n\nWe will never ask for your card number, bank details, Social Security number or insurance member ID by text message or email. If you receive a message like that which claims to come from us, do not reply to it, and call the front desk on (212) 555-0142.\n\n## Changing your phone number or email address\n\nTell the front desk at check-in, or update the contact section of Form PR-1 at the self-check-in kiosk. Reminders are sent to the phone number we hold when the reminder goes out.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2739,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.29576004,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": " room has to be prepared and cleaned between patients.\n\n## If the clinic is running late\n\nSometimes an earlier appointment takes longer than planned. If your practitioner is running more than 20 minut",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2740,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.2776901,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Appointment reminders and messages from the clinic\n\n## Text message reminders\n\nWe send a reminder by text message 48 hours before your appointment and another 2 hours before it. Our messages always ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2741,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.26311198,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": " your last name and date of birth. The kiosk cannot take payments: any copay or self-pay amount is paid at the front desk.\n\n## Language interpreters\n\nFree telephone interpreting is available in more t",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2739,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.25689805,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Running late\n\n## If you are running late\n\nCall the front desk on (212) 555-0142 as soon as you know you will be late, so we can tell the practitioner and plan around it. The phone line is answered M",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2726,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.2539514,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Do I need a referral from a primary care doctor to book with a specialist?\nAnswer: You can book a visit with any of our practitioners without a referral.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2727,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.25148338,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I bring to my first appointment?\nAnswer: Please bring a valid photo ID, your insurance card, and any relevant prior lab or test results related to your case.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2741,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.24193321,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n\n## Registering as a new patient\n\nNew patients fill in three forms at their first visit:\n\n- Form PR-1, New Patient Registration: your contact details, emergency contact a",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2735,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.23631701,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "re not in-network with Blue Essentials HMO or Blue Advantage HMO plans, because those plans only cover care from their own medical groups.\n\n## Aetna\n\nWe are in-network with Aetna Choice POS II and Aet",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2737,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.23581693,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Preparing for tests at the clinic\n\nSome tests are done at the clinic during a regular appointment. This guide explains how to prepare for each of them. If your doctor has given you different instruc",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2743,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.22935325,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "hree weeks apart. We do not remove skin tags, moles or other skin lesions for cosmetic reasons.\n\n## Medical examinations for work, driving and sport\n\nWe do not carry out commercial driver (DOT) medica",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2737,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.22488302,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "have been asked to bring a urine sample, collect a sterile container from the front desk beforehand; household containers can contaminate the sample. Unless you were told otherwise, collect the first ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2729,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.22440627,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Which health insurance plans do you accept?\nAnswer: We accept most major insurance providers, including Blue Cross Blue Shield, Aetna, Cigna, UnitedHealthcare, and Medicare. If you're unsure",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2730,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.2224727,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I do if my insurance isn't listed or I am out-of-network?\nAnswer: You can pay out-of-pocket for your visit, and we can provide you with an itemized receipt to submit to your insu",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2731,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.22094709,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: How much will my visit cost if I am paying out-of-pocket?\nAnswer: Out-of-pocket rates are $120 for a General Practitioner (GP) visit, $180 for a Dentist appointment, and $160 for all other s",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2744,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.21959351,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n\nYour itemized receipt lists each procedure done at your visit by its billing code. Medical procedures use five-digit CPT codes, and dental procedures use CDT cod",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2742,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.21611875,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "ltation for your personal use, as long as you tell the practitioner before you start. Staff and other patients must not be recorded or photographed.\n\n## How long we keep records\n\nWe keep adult medical",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2735,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.21493536,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n\nThis guide lists, plan by plan, the health insurance plans we are in-network with. Insurance companies sell many plans under one brand name, and being in-network with a company",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2735,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.21174781,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": " is not in-network. AARP Medicare Advantage plans from UnitedHealthcare are in-network when the plan is a PPO, and not in-network when it is an HMO.\n\n## Medicare and Medicaid\n\nWe accept Original Medic",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2738,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.19658494,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n\n## Seasonal flu vaccine\n\nWe give the flu vaccine every year from the start of September until the end of March. Patients aged 65 and over are offered a high-dose vaccine (Fluzone High-",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2738,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.19574153,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "vaccine $35, high-dose flu vaccine $70, Tdap $55, hepatitis A $85 per dose, typhoid injection $90, oral typhoid course $95, hepatitis B $70 per dose. They are the price of the vaccine itself, and are ",
          "text_truncated": true
        }
      ],
